do-3:claude:i3:clause:ci-retention-conditions"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:impact-cover","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:validity-dependency","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"stated-formula","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse"],"statement":"S_Δ = { t : D*(t) intersects I(Δ) }.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:ci-selection"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation"],"statement":"A construction binds A, the current state of Transitions above with its account, and Z, the destination as a predicate over realised states that includes the acceptance conditions of the selected outcome.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:cr-binds-a-z"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation"],"statement":"Completion requires sufficient evidence against Z, including its acceptance conditions; exhaustion or an unresolved attempt proves neither completion nor impossibility (P5, P6).","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:cr-completion-evidence"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:diagnosis-cause","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation"],"statement":"Diagnosis distinguishes four causes: a defective realisation, an inadequate governing requirement or design, an inaccurate predictive model, and insufficient observation.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:cr-four-causes"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation"],"statement":"Recursive and repeated work distinguish four claims: preservation, that an invariant or obligation is kept through the steps; progress, that the work moves towards Z on evidence; termination; and outcome satisfaction.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:cr-four-claims"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation"],"statement":"A lawful construction can remain incomplete or fail to reach Z, and lawfulness establishes neither delivery nor optimality.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:cr-lawful-not-delivery"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:diagnosis-cause","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation"],"statement":"A prediction error alone does not decide whether the required outcome holds.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:cr-prediction-error"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:support-kind","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"discharged-argument","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support-kind"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#formal-representation"],"statement":"Finite examples do not prove the universal implications above.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:fr-finite-examples"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"literal":"recovered: P0's standing in FOUNDATIONS §3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P0 Bounded construction. A finite actor realises a selected outer contract through steps. Each step's selected context fits the actor's envelope.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P1 Interpretation. Subject, representation and interpretation are distinct; meaning holds within a declared context through a declared contract.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P2 Purpose. A selected outcome defines adequacy; interfaces inherit material obligations from the transformation they serve.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P3 Identity. An object's identity is declared (authority, kind, value) and survives admissible change; a boundary is a claim with a proof obligation.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"literal":"only when the first's result type and judgment satisfy the second's exact declared domain and preconditions","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:condition"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P4a Typed composition. Two steps compose only when the first's result type and judgment satisfy the second's exact declared domain and preconditions.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p4a"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P4b Conservation of step-produced facts. Judgments, residuals, observations and authority decisions the outer contract needs are recorded by the step that produced them.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p4b"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P5 Totality. A step can meet a condition outside its context (P0's open-world premise), and it cannot report success on one (P6).","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P6 Justification and authority. Definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports a claim on a basis; authority permits or disposes within scope.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clau